<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kontor</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hanseatic Kontor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A Kontor was a foreign trading post of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>, a self-governing community of German merchants with its own aldermen, statutes, treasury and court. The four main Kontore were at Novgorod (the Peterhof), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergen">Bergen</a> (the German Wharf, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bryggen">Bryggen</a>), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> (the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steelyard">Steelyard</a>). They secured trade privileges from local rulers and imposed strict discipline on resident merchants.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kontor.jpg" alt="Kontor" width="320" height="307" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown, probably working in Bremen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hansehausantwerpen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
